        ("What has words, but never speaks?", "A book", ["A radio", "A mime", "A parrot"], "Printed books contain written words without vocal apparatus."),
        ("What can run, but never walks; has a bed, but never sleeps; has a mouth, but never talks?", "A river", ["A clock", "A car", "A computer"], "A river runs downstream, rests in a riverbed, and empties at its river mouth."),
        ("What has a head and a tail, but no body?", "A coin", ["A snake", "A comet", "A kite"], "A metal coin has 'heads' on the obverse and 'tails' on the reverse."),
        ("If there are three apples and you take away two, how many apples do you have?", "2 apples", ["1 apple", "3 apples", "0 apples"], "You took 2 apples, so you have the 2 apples you took."),
        ("A plane crashes exactly on the border between the US and Canada. Where do they bury the survivors?", "You do not bury survivors", ["In the US", "In Canada", "On the border"], "Survivors are living persons; they are not buried."),
        ("What gets sharper the more you use it?", "Your brain", ["A pencil", "A kitchen knife", "A scissors"], "Cognitive mental faculties improve and sharpen with frequent exercise."),
        ("How far can a dog run into the woods?", "Halfway, because after that the dog is running out of the woods", ["All the way", "Until it gets tired", "1 mile"], "Once the dog reaches the midpoint of the woods, it begins exiting the woods."),
