        ("What part of speech connects words, phrases, or clauses (such as 'and', 'but', or 'or')?", "Conjunction", ["Preposition", "Interjection", "Adverb"], "Coordinating conjunctions join grammatically equal syntactic elements."),
        ("In the sentence 'They arrived at the station before noon', what part of speech is 'at'?", "Preposition", ["Conjunction", "Adverb", "Pronoun"], "'At' is a preposition expressing spatial or temporal relationship."),
        ("Which word in the sentence 'Ouch! That hot pan burned my finger' is an interjection?", "Ouch", ["That", "Hot", "Burned"], "'Ouch' is an exclamatory interjection expressing sudden physical sensation."),
        ("In the sentence 'Knowledge is power', what part of speech is 'knowledge'?", "Noun (abstract noun)", ["Verb", "Adjective", "Pronoun"], "'Knowledge' names an abstract concept, functioning as the subject noun."),
        ("What type of pronoun replaces a specific person or thing (such as 'he', 'she', or 'it')?", "Personal pronoun", ["Demonstrative pronoun", "Relative pronoun", "Indefinite pronoun"], "Personal pronouns substitute for specific grammatical persons."),
        ("In the sentence 'She took herself to the doctor', what type of pronoun is 'herself'?", "Reflexive pronoun", ["Relative pronoun", "Demonstrative pronoun", "Interrogative pronoun"], "'Herself' refers back to the subject 'she' as the direct object."),
        ("Which word is an intransitive verb in the sentence 'The tired baby slept peacefully'?", "Slept", ["Tired", "Baby", "Peacefully"], "'Slept' expresses an action that does not take a direct object."),
        ("In the sentence 'Running is excellent cardiovascular exercise', what grammatical role does 'Running' serve?", "Gerund (noun)", ["Present participle verb", "Adjective", "Infinitive"], "A gerund is a verb ending in -ing functioning as a noun subject."),
        ("In the sentence 'I want to travel around the world', what is 'to travel'?", "Infinitive verb phrase", ["Gerund", "Participle", "Prepositional phrase"], "'To travel' is the base form of the verb preceded by 'to', acting as an infinitive."),
        ("In the sentence 'This book belongs to me', what part of speech is 'This'?", "Demonstrative adjective (determiner)", ["Demonstrative pronoun", "Adverb", "Noun"], "'This' modifies the noun 'book' directly, functioning as a demonstrative determiner."),
        ("In the phrase 'an extraordinarily talented musician', what part of speech is 'extraordinarily'?", "Adverb", ["Adjective", "Noun", "Conjunction"], "'Extraordinarily' modifies the adjective 'talented', making it an adverb."),
        ("Which word is a collective noun?", "Flock", ["Bird", "Flying", "Feathered"], "'Flock' refers to a group or collection of individual animals as a single unit."),
        ("What type of verb is 'seem' in the sentence 'The clouds seem heavy today'?", "Linking verb (copula)", ["Action verb", "Auxiliary verb", "Modal verb"], "Linking verbs connect the subject to a subject complement without expressing action."),
        ("In the sentence 'Neither the teacher nor the students were ready', what kind of conjunction is 'neither...nor'?", "Correlative conjunction", ["Coordinating conjunction", "Subordinating conjunction", "Adverbial conjunction"], "Correlative conjunctions work in tandem pairs to join sentence elements."),
        ("In the sentence 'Although it rained, we enjoyed the picnic', what part of speech is 'Although'?", "Subordinating conjunction", ["Preposition", "Coordinating conjunction", "Relative pronoun"], "'Although' introduces a dependent adverbial clause of concession."),
        ("What part of speech is 'under' in the phrase 'sleeping under the stars'?", "Preposition", ["Adverb", "Conjunction", "Adjective"], "'Under' relates 'sleeping' to the noun object 'the stars'."),
        ("In the sentence 'She gave him a warm smile', what grammatical function does 'him' serve?", "Indirect object", ["Direct object", "Subject", "Predicate noun"], "'Him' receives the direct object ('a warm smile')."),
        ("In the sentence 'The chef baked fresh bread', what grammatical function does 'fresh bread' serve?", "Direct object", ["Subject", "Indirect object", "Subject complement"], "'Fresh bread' directly receives the action of the transitive verb 'baked'."),
        ("Which word in the sentence 'He speaks Spanish very fluently' is an adverb modifying another adverb?", "Very", ["Spanish", "Speaks", "Fluently"], "'Very' is an intensifier adverb modifying the adverb 'fluently'."),
        ("What type of noun is 'committee'?", "Collective noun", ["Proper noun", "Abstract noun", "Mass noun"], "'Committee' denotes a group of people functioning as a singular body."),
        ("In the sentence 'Paris is the capital of France', what type of nouns are 'Paris' and 'France'?", "Proper nouns", ["Common nouns", "Abstract nouns", "Collective nouns"], "Names of specific unique entities are proper nouns and are capitalized."),
        ("What is the comparative form of the adjective 'good'?", "Better", ["Gooder", "Best", "More good"], "'Good' is an irregular adjective; its comparative form is 'better' and superlative is 'best'."),
        ("What is the superlative form of the adjective 'bad'?", "Worst", ["Worse", "Baddest", "Most bad"], "'Bad' is irregular; comparative is 'worse' and superlative is 'worst'."),
        ("In the sentence 'The dog wagged its tail', what part of speech is 'its'?", "Possessive determiner/adjective", ["Contraction of it is", "Personal pronoun", "Adverb"], "'Its' indicates possession without an apostrophe, modifying 'tail'."),
        ("Which of the following is a modal auxiliary verb?", "Should", ["Running", "Brightly", "Underneath"], "Modal verbs (can, could, may, might, must, shall, should, will, would) express modality."),
        ("What is the past participle of the irregular verb 'swim'?", "Swum", ["Swam", "Swimmed", "Swimming"], "Conjugation: present swim, simple past swam, past participle swum."),
        ("What is the past participle of the irregular verb 'freeze'?", "Frozen", ["Froze", "Freezed", "Freezing"], "Conjugation: freeze, froze, frozen."),
        ("What is the past participle of the irregular verb 'write'?", "Written", ["Wrote", "Writed", "Writing"], "Conjugation: write, wrote, written."),
        ("In the sentence 'The broken vase could not be repaired', what is 'broken'?", "Past participle functioning as an adjective", ["Gerund", "Infinitive", "Adverb"], "'Broken' is a participial adjective modifying the noun 'vase'."),
        ("Which word is an indefinite pronoun in 'Someone left their umbrella in the hallway'?", "Someone", ["Left", "Their", "Umbrella"], "'Someone' refers to an unspecified person, functioning as an indefinite pronoun."),
